    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Honestly, I never really clicked with it back in school. It felt too rigid and abstract for someone like me who loves history or computer science instead. I prefer understanding things through stories or practical use rather than pure formulas. While I can follow basic calculations, the deeper theoretical stuff always left me feeling disconnected and unsure about its real value to my daily life.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Sometimes, yes. When someone brings up complex math concepts, I immediately feel a knot in my stomach. My low openness to experience makes it hard to embrace new abstract ideas, and past negative experiences with rigid teaching styles have made me hesitant to engage. It's not that I fear failure, but rather the pressure of performing in a way that doesn't align with my natural learning style.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "No, I haven't actually used AI for this purpose. To be honest, I'm not very tech-savvy when it comes to academic tools and prefer sticking to what I know. My low conscientiousness might mean I don't seek out these resources as actively as others do. However, I would admit that if someone explained how it could help me without making things more complicated, I might give it a try.",
