    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y equals f of x?": "Okay, think of it like finding where a hill flattens out. First, take the derivative of your function f(x). This gives you the slope at any point. Then set that derivative equal to zero because horizontal lines have no slope. Solve this new equation for x values, and plug them back into the original function to get y coordinates. Those points are where nothing is changing direction.",
